" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Ethiopian government forces have made advances against a northern rebel group. Renewed fighting has raised fears the conflict could spill over into the wider region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Peru: Fire burning on road to Machu Picchu kills 1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f20fc924163ab3633d4fa5b3caf5fe792f3c5940b9b9eaab7cb096a95427494</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:04:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T02:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peru-fire-burning-on-road-to-machu-picchu-kills-1/a-79534344--e801992ff38b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peru-fire-burning-on-road-to-machu-picchu-kills-1/a-79534344?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One person has died and two others have suffered burns in a fire near the main access route to the historic sanctuary of Machu Picchu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's 2026 presidential election is kicking off with polls showing Lula and Bolsonaro nearly tied.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70ccd656ec6c031c22804fafa0db3eef64cb642f2dfa6a5c1b4089fef489b45</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T01:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-2026-presidential-election-is-kicking-off-with-polls-showing-lula-and-bolsonaro-nearly-tied/a-79533857--1a3954f96db5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-2026-presidential-election-is-kicking-off-with-polls-showing-lula-and-bolsonaro-nearly-tied/a-79533857?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former far-right populist President Jair Bolsonaro, is taking on incumbent left-wing President Lula da Silva. Polls show the first round of voting will likely lead to a runoff.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI giants 'not being nearly careful enough,' warns outgoing OpenAI safety engineer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df2861d954fc0ddd98c4839dc79ce162e2dc4fc8fa58da4659a1d0144fac5a19</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:05:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T21:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-giants-not-being-nearly-careful-enough-warns-outgoing-openai-safety-engineer/a-79533080--b451aed5afe0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-giants-not-being-nearly-careful-enough-warns-outgoing-openai-safety-engineer/a-79533080?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Days after US President Donald Trump signed a voluntary pact with artificial intelligence giants, a former OpenAI worker said his industry needs the same safeguards as nuclear power or aviation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan vs. Afghanistan: From allies and neighbors to war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3af2771a52f3ea4008986056ec8b277503281ef7650f4186035007d263378633</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T18:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-vs-afghanistan-from-allies-and-neighbors-to-war/a-79532115--d94d668c07cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-vs-afghanistan-from-allies-and-neighbors-to-war/a-79532115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For years, Pakistan supported the Taliban in Afghanistan. But now Pakistan is bombing its neighbor. How the former allies became adversaries and why negotiations keep failing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee's prison chief resigns after botched execution of murderer Christa Pike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4634ab0b6395ef38b171ccb2b5738c3a7010122046d751e4db5cd95ca9a73fd6</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T18:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennessee-s-prison-chief-resigns-after-botched-execution-of-murderer-christa-pike/a-79532481--aa48d2d74320.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennessee-s-prison-chief-resigns-after-botched-execution-of-murderer-christa-pike/a-79532481?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prison commissioner Frank Strada insisted his team followed protocol, even after two doses of anesthetic failed to kill convicted murderer Christa Pike. He is set to leave his post this month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Latvia: Ruling party leads in exit polls amid populist gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe23ac73bb1b5b1b9693e3265f6b6f91b14cc00e1600c3829a5168d115df9f9</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/latvia-ruling-party-leads-in-exit-polls-amid-populist-gains/a-79527253--37a89168d1aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latvia-ruling-party-leads-in-exit-polls-amid-populist-gains/a-79527253?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to an exit poll by public broadcaster LSM, Latvian Prime Minister Andris Kulbergs' centerist party, United List, was projected to win 35.6% of the vote.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine to step up oil attacks as Russia hits Kyiv bridges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:912e738e1c2e009ad8bbb90c1248ebaa6cb7ab823144cce217b86316a2d6b7ac</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-to-step-up-oil-attacks-as-russia-hits-kyiv-bridges/a-79527753--849b2892c79a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-to-step-up-oil-attacks-as-russia-hits-kyiv-bridges/a-79527753?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Moscow intensifies attacks on Kyiv and other cities, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has vowed to hit Russian energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK remands 2 Iranians over alleged antisemitic terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2303205dfba7660eb5ace8a5a2bee9a4f44d55ade9e6cc05e4cfe3c55136d76</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T16:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184--b38b3689556f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pair were arrested on the eve of Yom Kippur and later charged with plotting to attack Jewish targets in Manchester.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Massive protests after housing bills voted down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc86c0a4713a37dccc271c4a045bf7f964070babd1ecd58b621ee917c59b0665</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-massive-protests-after-housing-bills-voted-down/a-79532124--ca04770eabd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-massive-protests-after-housing-bills-voted-down/a-79532124?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Organizers estimated that 500,000 people turned out in the streets of Madrid to demand affordable housing. Similar protests were held in around 50 other Spanish cities.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greece returns remains of Czar Samuel to Bulgaria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78386e5627a45cd574cdb36a49c6309f2c16aca45381844d2acc8d6d0d205ebc</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-returns-remains-of-czar-samuel-to-bulgaria/a-79530104--e4eab7810bf7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-returns-remains-of-czar-samuel-to-bulgaria/a-79530104?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A warrior emperor who ruled the Bulgarian Empire in the Middle Ages, Czar Samuel is a symbol of Bulgarian national identity. But his remains have been in Greece for decades – and he is also claimed by North Macedonia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Floods leave 102-year-old woman dead in southeast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a92aa0192e81043b857eef68de82ca0968dfc843bb04b94c5e04ca9ee8fa8f17</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-floods-leave-102-year-old-woman-dead-in-southeast/a-79529983--d4597da5456b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-floods-leave-102-year-old-woman-dead-in-southeast/a-79529983?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Spain rescued some 90 people after heavy rain sparked flooding in the town of Madrigueras. Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez expressed his condolences to the family of a 102-year-old woman who died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>On German Unity Day, Steinmeier laments 'bitter setbacks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee6372dc7c8fb097424e1b342a81360d884fcff47fb476246ac24e0a56fe2960</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T10:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-german-unity-day-steinmeier-laments-bitter-setbacks/live-79528092--4d5945f39bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-german-unity-day-steinmeier-laments-bitter-setbacks/live-79528092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's president has used his final Unity Day speech to warn the hopes of the reunification era have suffered "bitter setbacks." DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cockroach Janta Party announces Delhi march for October 10, calls for election chief's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6472fe6c8e566e66830c843cd39f05925b24ebb2e7cf0d5c77572e787c7ce588</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T10:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-janta-party-announces-delhi-march-for-october-10-calls-for-election-chief-s-res/live-79527537--f1f6a3f98858.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-janta-party-announces-delhi-march-for-october-10-calls-for-election-chief-s-resignation/live-79527537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Cockroach Janta Party has called for a protest in Delhi if Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar does not resign. After the Indian men's cricket team struck gold, all eyes are on their hockey counterparts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai co-pilot attempted 'terrorist attack,' UAE says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7695adae8b830157f48381c5616ef51401e4d0829d058b0b46b5bcde61675f7</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-co-pilot-attempted-terrorist-attack-uae-says/a-79526641--5d350a043c31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-co-pilot-attempted-terrorist-attack-uae-says/a-79526641?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man, who stabbed his fellow pilot on an Israel-bound Flydubai flight, was reportedly barred from flying in his native Oman over security concerns.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:841180c718fa51f1c1908839b2ef2c340b78075306085fb48b955acfa0e05667</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina is still shaped by war, separatism, EU ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9cc478ab179d1c4dc4c2d1e0800571be0e41a8dcc8a4f22b64ba4c0980f927d</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557--c6b59bb6d492.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia and Herzegovina is governed by a system established after the Bosnian war — more than 30 years ago. Ethnic divisions, a complex administration and European integration all shape the country's political reality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German reunification: How inequality is shaping a new East German identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:648a5900508b767b15c395c87456c509a06b8dbf41ef9b15d4069b45c93e8775</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T04:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541--28106a765624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new study highlights persistent structural disparities in wealth and leadership positions between East and West Germany, 36 years after reunification.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Australia: Car crashes into rugby fans, 10 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b70ce2a99b4862fe786f9a6a173ec6f6e5a68a74186c0e5858808234ecf3dea</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T04:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-car-crashes-into-rugby-fans-10-injured/a-79526643--1bdc3d304c0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-car-crashes-into-rugby-fans-10-injured/a-79526643?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The driver has been identified as an 18-year-old man who is said to have been "revving" when he lost control of his car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US, Australia suspend consular services in Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f835e0540d389c987d8ff68596db426add55657761eadbfc8d5daf338051db5</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T02:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-australia-suspend-consular-services-in-brazil/a-79526311--0fa29ec750af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-australia-suspend-consular-services-in-brazil/a-79526311?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US and Australia have announced a halt to their consular services in Brazil beginning Friday. The news comes two days before Brazilians head to the polls to vote in the high-stakes presidential election.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
